{
  "abstract": "Three classical reconstruction theorems: a disconnected graph on at least three vertices is determined by its vertex deck (Kelly 1957); a graph with m > C(n,2)/2 edges (Lovász 1972) or with n! < 2^(m−1) (Müller 1977) is determined by its edge deck.",
